 and Mercedes and Range Rovers,

89
00:03:17,580 --> 00:03:19,740
 like cars that have nicer interiors

90
00:03:19,740 --> 00:03:21,620
 than the interior of my apartment, you know?

91
00:03:21,620 --> 00:03:25,100
 And as I get out of my car and I slowly make my way inside,

92
00:03:25,100 --> 00:03:27,420
 I see all of the people coming in alongside me.

93
00:03:27,420 --> 00:03:28,980
 And I guess I was a little bit underdressed

94
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:31,580
 because they were all dressed to the nines.

95
00:03:31,580 --> 00:03:33,060
 Ladies were in like silk dresses

96
00:03:33,060 --> 00:03:34,820
 and guys were in black tuxes.

97
00:03:34,820 --> 00:03:36,620
 And we make our way in and bag check.

98
00:03:36,620 --> 00:03:39,020
 It's got Gucci and Louis and all the fam there.

99
00:03:39,020 --> 00:03:40,180
 And as I'm walking around,

100
00:03:40,180 --> 00:03:41,980
 I just see all the guys that they've got,

101
00:03:41,980 --> 00:03:44,540
 like Rolexes and Omegas hanging off their wrists.

102
00:03:44,540 --> 00:03:46,500
 I don't know about you, like the watch that I wear,

103
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:47,940
 it tells me the time.

104
00:03:47,940 --> 00:03:50,620
 The watch that they wear tells them their net worth,

105
00:03:50,620 --> 00:03:53,460
 you know, and as we're walking across campus,

106
00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:55,460
 like campus is just like humming

107
00:03:55,460 --> 00:03:56,620
 because so many people are excited.

108
00:03:56,620 --> 00:03:59,700
 Like the place looks immaculate, it's beautiful.

109
00:03:59,700 --> 00:04:02,100
 But there's also like the sweet sound of music

110
00:04:02,100 --> 00:04:03,540
 in every corner you go.

111
00:04:03,540 --> 00:04:04,540
 Like you walk over here

112
00:04:04,540 --> 00:04:05,780
 and there's a girl who's singing soul

113
00:04:05,780 --> 00:04:06,860
 and you walk over here

114
00:04:06,860 --> 00:04:08,500
 and there's a guy who's singing the blues

115
00:04:08,500 --> 00:04:09,340
 and you walk over here

116
00:04:09,340 --> 00:04:12,100
 and they've got like slowed down 2000s covers going on.

117
00:04:12,100 --> 00:04:12,940
 You know what I'm talking about?

118
00:04:12,940 --> 00:04:14,540
 Like the music that sounds way more sophisticated

119
00:04:14,540 --> 00:04:15,380
 than it actually is

120
00:04:15,380 --> 00:04:18,020
 because lyrically it's still just Usher.

121
00:04:18,020 --> 00:04:19,860
 That's what was happening

122
00:04:19,860 --> 00:04:21,460
 before I ever even got to the party

123
00:04:21,460 --> 00:04:23,900
 'cause this is just in the office space

124
00:04:23,900 --> 00:04:25,300
 that they were commissioning,

125
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:27,580
 but outside on the grand lawn,

126
00:04:27,580 --> 00:04:29,740
 a lawn which was actually seeded

127
00:04:29,740 --> 00:04:31,940
 with the very same grass from Kyle Field itself.

128
00:04:31,940 --> 00:04:34,740
 Like that's how ridiculous this thing was.

129
00:04:34,740 --> 00:04:39,740
 I make my way under this like, this massive white tent.

130
00:04:39,740 --> 00:04:43,860
 And as I step under the tent, everything changes.

131
00:04:43,860 --> 00:04:45,860
 Like there are crystal chandeliers

132
00:04:45,860 --> 00:04:49,380
 hanging all across the skyline.

133
00:04:49,380 --> 00:04:53,660
 And then there's a giant marble checker dance floor

134
00:04:53,660 --> 00:04:55,660
 and a 12 piece jazz band.

135
00:04:55,660 --> 00:04:58,660
 And there are, there's so much food,

136
00:04:58,660 --> 00:05:00,540
 like food like you would not believe

137
00:05:00,540 --> 00:05:05,540
 because they had invited the three best chefs in the city

138
00:05:05,540 --> 00:05:08,660
 to prep for us whatever it is was their thing.

139
00:05:08,660 --> 00:05:12,020
 Like these are the people that you would take,

140
00:05:12,020 --> 00:05:15,860
 like big business deals to sign on the dotted line.

141
00:05:15,860 --> 00:05:17,060
 You would take a girl

142
00:05:17,060 --> 00:05:18,860
 if you were trying to make a really good impression

143
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:20,300
 or you would take some clients

144
00:05:20,300 --> 00:05:21,620
 if you were trying to appear more successful

145
00:05:21,620 --> 00:05:22,460
 than you actually were.

146
00:05:22,460 --> 00:05:24,100
 These were the restaurants that these guys ran

147
00:05:24,100 --> 00:05:28,300
 and they were all there at the same time serving us.

148
00:05:28,300 --> 00:05:31,100
 One of them, he was like a specialist in seafood.

149
00:05:31,100 --> 00:05:33,860
 And so he had flown all of the seafood in from Maine.

150
00:05:33,860 --> 00:05:35,980
 Another one, he's back there carving steak

151
00:05:35,980 --> 00:05:37,100
 straight out of Florence.

152
00:05:37,100 --> 00:05:39,620
 And then another one is like constructing

153
00:05:39,620 --> 00:05:44,620
 these sushi towers, not sushi boats, sushi towers.

154
00:05:45,480 --> 00:05:49,140
 And it hit me in that moment as I watched him do his work.

155
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:52,260
 This is my job.

156
00:05:52,260 --> 00:05:53,860
 This is where I work.

157
00:05:53,860 --> 00:05:55,300
 This is the greatest thing ever.

158
00:05:55,300 --> 00:05:57,260
 Like I knew I'd be earning a paycheck.

159
00:05:57,260 --> 00:05:59,660
 I didn't know that I was gonna get a guest spot

160
00:05:59,660 --> 00:06:01,540
 in the second season of Succession.

161
00:06:01,540 --> 00:06:05,580
 Like this was unlike anything I had ever imagined.

162
00:06:05,580 --> 00:06:08,900
 Like I knew I was living the dream

163
00:06:08,900 --> 00:06:12,640
 and yet I realized it wasn't quite as dreamy as I expected

164
00:06:12,640 --> 00:06:13,780
 because right around the time

165
00:06:13,780 --> 00:06:16,140
 as I was shoveling in my third plate of lobster mac and cheese

166
00:06:16,140 --> 00:06:19,860
 I remember I passed by a group of coworkers

167
00:06:19,860 --> 00:06:23,020
 that had sort of like a common beard,

168
00:06:23,020 --> 00:06:24,780
 a conference room space.

169
00:06:24,780 --> 00:06:27,460
 And they weren't dressed to the nines like the rest of us.

170
00:06:27,460 --> 00:06:29,060
 They weren't dancing the night away.

171
00:06:29,060 --> 00:06:30,300
 They weren't drinking the drinks.

172
00:06:30,300 --> 00:06:32,380
 They definitely weren't sampling the food.

173
00:06:32,380 --> 00:06:35,420
 They were in there and they were working of all things.

174
00:06:35,420 --> 00:06:37,340
 Like you're working at a time like this.

175
00:06:37,340 --> 00:06:38,180
 Are you kidding me?

176
00:06:38,180 --> 00:06:40,220
 Like the sushi towers are right there

177
00:06:40,220 --> 00:06:42,060
 and you're working in this moment.

178
00:06:42,060 --> 00:06:43,740
 Like I don't care about your work ethic.

179
00:06:43,740 --> 00:06:45,860
 This is a cry for help.

180
00:06:45,860 --> 00:06:47,540
 This is the craziest thing I've ever seen.

181
00:06:47,540 --> 00:06:49,940
 What do you think you're doing?

182
00:06:49,940 --> 00:06:53,460
 And yet, as I was so baffled beyond belief

183
00:06:53,460 --> 00:06:56,140
 that there were a group of people there working,

184
00:06:56,140 --> 00:06:57,220
 one of the guys from my team

185
00:06:57,220 --> 00:06:58,780
 who was walking around with me,

186
00:06:58,780 --> 00:06:59,800
 he looked at me and he said,

187
00:06:59,800 --> 00:07:02,340
 "Well, I guess it's true.

188
00:07:02,340 --> 00:07:04,940
 "The party's gotta end for all of us at some point."

189
00:07:04,940 --> 00:07:07,700
 And you know what?

190
00:07:07,700 --> 00:07:08,540
 He was right.

191
00:07:08,540 --> 00:07:11,300
 He was right.

192
00:07:11,300 --> 00:07:13,940
 Like eventually the music did end.

193
00:07:13,940 --> 00:07:15,820
 The lights did come up.

194
00:07:15,820 --> 00:07:17,700
 The drinks did drain.

195
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:20,040
 The stage got packed back in.

196
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:21,820
 The band left.

197
00:07:21,820 --> 00:07:23,540
 The tent came down.

198
00:07:23,540 --> 00:07:25,460
 And whether it was that Saturday night

199
00:07:25,460 --> 00:07:27,900
 that people decided to stop and join the party

200
00:07:27,900 --> 00:07:30,780
 or was that Monday morning when everybody else showed up,

201
00:07:30,780 --> 00:07:32,540
 we all knew we were gonna be back in

202
00:07:32,540 --> 00:07:34,740
 building spreadsheets and answering emails

203
00:07:34,740 --> 00:07:37,660
 and rising and grinding the way that we always did

204
00:07:37,660 --> 00:07:39,380
 because here's the truth.

205
00:07:39,380 --> 00:07:41,640
 Pleasure is nice,

206
00:07:41,640 --> 00:07:45,920
 but pleasure is never permanent.

207
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:47,780
 Pleasure is never permanent,

208
00:07:47,780 --> 00:07:52,100
 which is why so many people spend their lives chasing it.

209
00:07:52,100 --> 00:07:54,900
 I remember when I was in college ministry

210
00:07:54,900 --> 00:07:56,540
 at Texas A&M University,

211
00:07:56,540 --> 00:07:58,540
 there was a guy there who I knew,

212
00:07:58,540 --> 00:08:00,060
 he's a student in our ministry.

213
00:08:00,060 --> 00:08:01,980
 Every single week he would go out

214
00:08:01,980 --> 00:08:04,840
 and he would just get hammered.

215
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:07,320
 And I was like, "Nick, what are you doing?

216
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:10,560
 "Like, why do you do this to yourself every single week?"

217
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:12,240
 Granted, he didn't know Jesus.

218
00:08:12,240 --> 00:08:14,480
 And so he looked at me and he was like,

219
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:18,100
 "Because last Friday was last week, bro."

220
00:08:18,100 --> 00:08:19,740
 And what was he saying?

221
00:08:19,740 --> 00:08:23,540
 He was like, "Pleasure is in the past.

222
00:08:23,540 --> 00:08:24,840
 "Like, it's not right now.

223
00:08:24,840 --> 00:08:26,380
 "It's something that happened back then.

224
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:28,060
 "And man, it was awesome at that time,

225
00:08:28,060 --> 00:08:29,460
 "but now I've gotta get back out there.

226
00:08:29,460 --> 00:08:32,460
 "I've got to get to chasing it again.

227
00:08:32,460 --> 00:08:34,020
 "Like, there's another milestone to reach.

228
00:08:34,020 --> 00:08:35,480
 "There's another big night to have.

229
00:08:35,480 --> 00:08:37,540
 "There's another purchase to make.

230
00:08:37,540 --> 00:08:38,960
 "There's another trip to find.

231
00:08:38,960 --> 00:08:41,220
 "Like, this is the way that pleasure works in our lives.

232
00:08:41,220 --> 00:08:42,860
 "We chase after it.

233
00:08:42,860 --> 00:08:44,940
 "But here's the question I have for you.

234
00:08:44,940 --> 00:08:48,560
 "What happens when you get everything you want

235
00:08:48,560 --> 00:08:50,260
 "and it's still not enough?

236
00:08:50,260 --> 00:08:53,440
 "What happens in that moment?

237
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:56,200
 "Like, what if you get all the pleasure

238
00:08:56,200 --> 00:08:58,940
 "that your heart desires and you find out

239
00:08:58,940 --> 00:09:03,660
 "that pleasure isn't actually satisfying

240
00:09:03,660 --> 00:09:05,740
 "the deep longings of your soul?

241
00:09:05,740 --> 00:09:07,340
 "What do you do in that moment?"

242
00:09:07,340 --> 00:09:10,260
 Well, that's what I want to talk to you about,

243
00:09:10,260 --> 00:09:11,980
 because that's what the book of Ecclesiastes

244
00:09:11,980 --> 00:09:13,020
 is actually answering for.

245
00:09:13,020 --> 00:09:14,020
 So if you've got a Bible,

246
00:09:14,020 --> 00:09:17,200
 turn with me to Ecclesiastes chapter two.

247
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:18,220
 While you're doing that,

248
00:09:18,220 --> 00:09:22,060
 we've been in a series called Lovers,

249
00:09:22,060 --> 00:09:23,260
 not because it's a dating series

250
00:09:23,260 --> 00:09:25,340
 and not because we're just trying to bait and switch you,

251
00:09:25,340 --> 00:09:29,680
 but because we believe that everyone is going to be a lover

252
00:09:29,680 --> 00:09:32,540
 of something in life.

253
00:09:32,540 --> 00:09:36,200
 And yet there's only one thing worthy of loving in life,

254
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:37,980
 and that's God.

255
00:09:37,980 --> 00:09:39,060
 Paul says it like this.

256
00:09:39,060 --> 00:09:43,140
 He says specifically in 2 Timothy three, one through five,

257
00:09:43,140 --> 00:09:45,540
 which is where this series is birthed out at.

258
00:09:45,540 --> 00:09:49,400
 He says, "But understand this,

259
00:09:49,400 --> 00:09:50,520
 "that in the last days,

260
00:09:50,520 --> 00:09:52,900
 "there will come times of difficulty for people.

261
00:09:52,900 --> 00:09:54,340
 "They will be lovers of self."

262
00:09:54,340 --> 00:09:55,320
 We talked about that.

263
00:09:55,320 --> 00:09:56,160
 "Lovers of money."

264
00:09:56,160 --> 00:09:57,120
